# Medication Checker

## Overview

Medication Checker is a web application that allows users to search for medicine information using the OpenFDA Drug Label API. Users enter the generic name of a medicine and retrieve reliable information such as its description, warnings, dosage, and instructions for use. The application also allows users to filter the results and display only the information they are interested in, such as warnings, dosage, description, or instructions.

The application was built using Python, HTML, CSS, and JavaScript and is deployed on two web servers behind an HAProxy load balancer to improve availability and reliability.

---

# Problem Statement

People often need quick access to reliable medicine information before taking medication. Searching through multiple websites can be time-consuming and may lead to inaccurate or incomplete information.

Medication Checker provides a simple and user-friendly solution by retrieving official medicine information directly from the OpenFDA Drug Label API and allowing users to display only the information they need.

---

# Features

- Search medicines using their generic name
- View medicine description
- View medicine warnings
- View dosage information
- View instructions for use
- Filter results to display:
  - All information
  - Description only
  - Warnings only
  - Dosage only
  - Instructions only
- Handles invalid medicine names gracefully
- Handles OpenFDA API connection errors
- Responsive user interface
- Deployed on two web servers behind a HAProxy load balancer

---

